fun mergePage(cached: List<Post>, freshPage: List<Post>): List<Post> {
    val seenIds = cached.map { it.id }.toSet()
    val newPosts = freshPage.filterNot { it.id in seenIds }
    return cached + newPosts   // append only genuinely new items, preserve existing order
}
```

The de-duplication step matters because a naive 'just append whatever the API returned' merge can produce a duplicate if the same post appears in two overlapping page fetches — which happens more often than it sounds, especially if a cursor's position shifts slightly due to a post being deleted between two of the user's requests. Merging by ID, not by position, is what keeps the feed correct under that kind of real-world churn.
